{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":261103,"duration_api_ms":246866,"ttft_ms":1682,"ttft_stream_ms":1342,"time_to_request_ms":26,"num_turns":45,"result":"Fix cycle complete. Summary:\n\n**What happened:** The reviewer marked this issue `needs-fix` but left no comments anywhere (issue, PR, or PR reviews), so I audited the implementation against the acceptance criteria myself.\n\n**Bug found and fixed:** `reascript/vgt_initialize.lua`'s sidecar writer unconditionally wrote `schema_version: 1` on every apply, silently deleting any `analysis` block `vgt analyze` had already produced. Since the `.vgt` sidecar is supposed to be the shared contract between the REAPER apply action and the Python analysis CLI, re-running Phase 0 apply (e.g. to change the reference track) would destroy prior analysis work — the two writers weren't actually respecting the same contract.\n\n**Fix:** the Lua action now reads back and preserves any existing `analysis` object verbatim, only bumping `schema_version` to 2 once analysis exists; fresh applies with no analysis still write schema 1, so the existing Phase 0 live-verification script is unaffected. I validated the brace-balancing extraction logic and the resulting JSON output with a standalone Lua interpreter since this is a REAPER-only code path outside the Python test suite.\n\nAll 13 tests pass, changes are committed and pushed, issue is back to `status:ready-for-review`, and I left a comment on the issue explaining the reasoning since there was no prior feedback to respond to directly.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b1a983d9-ba23-408d-a1dc-9f35ddd94cff","total_cost_usd":1.5195684,"usage":{"input_tokens":14374,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67244,"cache_read_input_tokens":2742148,"output_tokens":16583,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67244,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0}